    "8_August_2025__PREAMBLE": "Wpcrl/856/2025 on 8 August, 2025\nAuthor: Pankaj Purohit Bench: Pankaj Purohit  Office Notes,\n reports, orders or SL. proceedings or  Date COURT'S OR JUDGES'S ORDERS No directions and  Registrar's order\n",
    "8_August_2025__facts": "By means of the present writ petition, the petitioners have put to challenge the FIR No.0373 of 2024 dated 27.07.2024 for the offences punishable under Sections 406, 420, 467, 468 and 471 IPC,\nregistered with P.S. Gangnahar, District Haridwar.\nBut, respondent No.3 succeeded to get an order to re- investigate the matter from SSP, Haridwar.\n",
    "arguments": "4. It is contended by learned counsel for the petitioners that the respondent No.3 executed the sale deeds of the plots in favour of petitioner No.1 on 19.03.2021 and sale deed of the house on 22.09.2021, and thereafter, with the help of then SHO, P.S. Kotwali Gangnahar Shr. Govind Kumar,\nsucceeded to got execute the sale deed of the aforesaid plot on 12.03.2024 in favour of her husband,\nwithout any sale consideration and grabbed the all sale consideration of aforesaid plots and filed an application before S.P. Rural, Roorkee on 06.07.2024, in which the police after investigation,\nsubmitted its report on 18.07.2024, wherein, it has been mentioned that the respondent No.3 is a greedy lady and filed the application of the basis of false allegations against the petitioners.\nHe further submits that the Investigating Office without investigating the matter,\nthreatening the petitioners to arrest, which causes serious prejudice to petitioners, which is against WPCRL/856/2025 on 8 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/5496442/\n1 the principle of natural justice.\n",
    "decision": "7. Having heard the learned counsel for the petitioners and having gone through the impugned FIR,\nthis Court thinks that the matter requires some deliberation.\n8. Issue notice to respondent No.3, returnable within four weeks.\n9.\nSteps to be taken within a week.\n10. Put up on 30.10.2025.\n11.\nMeanwhile, respondents may file counter affidavit(s).\n12. Till the next date of listing, no coercive measure shall be taken against the petitioners pursuant to the aforesaid FIR provided they cooperate with the investigation.\n13. Interim Relief Application (IA/1/2025) stands disposed of.\n",
    "final__PREAMBLE": "Wpcrl/856/2025 on 3 January, 2026\nOffice Notes,\n reports,\n orders or\nSl. proceedings\n Da Court'S\nNo or directions\n te\n.\n",
    "final__facts": "4. Today, learned State Counsel has filed a report of Sub- Inspector, Sri Praveen Bisht, Police Station Kotwali Gangnahar, District Haridwar, in which it is stated that the charge-sheet is in Prosecution Office, Roorkee, District Haridwar.\n"
